{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "axel-webhooks-collection",
    "name": "Axel Webhook Tester",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Synthetic requests for Axel source ingest. This public collection intentionally excludes operator endpoints and infrastructure credentials.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Import this file and `axel-webhooks.postman_environment.json`.\n2. Create a disposable source that receives synthetic test data only.\n3. Put its source ID and one-time token in the private environment.\n4. Send `Hello → 202` to confirm the setup.\n\nDo not reuse a production source, paste real webhook bodies into these requests, or share or export a populated environment. Rotate the disposable source token when testing is finished."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Hello",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Hello → 202",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Returns event_id (uuid v7)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.event_id).to.match(/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Returns received_at (ISO)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.received_at).to.match(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}T/);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "content-type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-axel-token", "value": "{{sourceToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event\": \"hello\",\n  \"sent_from\": \"postman\",\n  \"value\": 42\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/in/{{sourceId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["in", "{{sourceId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Minimal payload. Use this first to confirm `sourceId` + `sourceToken` are correct."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
