    {
      "name": "Batch & throughput",
      "description": "How to send 'many records at once' through Axel.\n\n**Important model note:** Axel ingests one event per POST. There's no native batch endpoint that splits an array into N events. You have two patterns:\n\n1. **One event with array body** — each request below sends a single event whose body happens to contain an array of records. Your destination connector receives one document/row per webhook (the whole array). This is the right model when you control both producer + consumer and want to amortize round-trip cost.\n2. **N events via Postman Collection Runner** — the **Run-runner sample** request below is configured for use with Postman's Runner: open it, hit *Run collection*, set iterations to 100, and Axel sees 100 distinct events. This is the right model for stress-testing or when each record is conceptually its own event.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Single event — array of 10 records",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "content-type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-axel-token", "value": "{{sourceToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"batch_id\": \"batch_postman_10\",\n  \"records\": [\n    { \"id\": 1, \"name\": \"alice\", \"amount\": 100 },\n    { \"id\": 2, \"name\": \"bob\",   \"amount\": 250 },\n    { \"id\": 3, \"name\": \"carol\", \"amount\": 175 },\n    { \"id\": 4, \"name\": \"dave\",  \"amount\": 320 },\n    { \"id\": 5, \"name\": \"erin\",  \"amount\": 412 },\n    { \"id\": 6, \"name\": \"frank\", \"amount\": 87  },\n    { \"id\": 7, \"name\": \"gina\",  \"amount\": 999 },\n    { \"id\": 8, \"name\": \"henry\", \"amount\": 50  },\n    { \"id\": 9, \"name\": \"iris\",  \"amount\": 720 },\n    { \"id\":10, \"name\": \"jack\",  \"amount\": 145 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/in/{{sourceId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["in", "{{sourceId}}"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Single event — top-level array (100 numbers)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Build a 100-element array of pseudo-records and stash on the request.",
                  "const records = Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, i) => ({",
                  "  id: i + 1,",
                  "  ts: new Date(Date.now() - (100 - i) * 1000).toISOString(),",
                  "  amount: Math.round(Math.random() * 10000) / 100",
                  "}));",
                  "pm.variables.set('batch100', JSON.stringify(records));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "content-type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-axel-token", "value": "{{sourceToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{{batch100}}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/in/{{sourceId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["in", "{{sourceId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Top-level array body. The pre-request script generates 100 records dynamically. Axel persists the whole array as one event in R2 and forwards it to your destination as one delivery."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Run-runner sample — fire many distinct events",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Create a unique payload per iteration so Axel sees N distinct events.",
                  "const i = pm.info.iteration ?? 0;",
                  "pm.variables.set('iterationIndex', i);",
                  "pm.variables.set('iterationTimestamp', new Date().toISOString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('202', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "content-type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-axel-token", "value": "{{sourceToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event\": \"runner_burst\",\n  \"iteration\": {{iterationIndex}},\n  \"sent_at\": \"{{iterationTimestamp}}\",\n  \"customer\": \"acme-load-test\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/in/{{sourceId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["in", "{{sourceId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Open Postman's **Collection Runner** (top-right ▶), select this request only, set **Iterations = 100** (or whatever you want), hit **Run**. Each iteration sends a distinct event to Axel. Watch the count climb on https://app.axelapp.ai/usage."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Edge cases / errors",
      "description": "Each of these intentionally violates the ingest contract. Tests assert the expected non-2xx status. If any of them stop returning the right code, something's broken in the worker.",
      "item": [
